.TH GPUBENCH-GUI 1 "September 2026" "GPUBench 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpubench-gui \- Graphical interface for GPU compute and hardware ray tracing benchmarking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpubench-gui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GPUBench GUI
is the graphical workstation profiler for GPUBench, built on a shared Vulkan 1.4 device, Dear ImGui 1.93 dynamic font baking, and ImPlot v1.1. It features live cross-platform hardware telemetry graphs (GPU clock, temperature, power, VRAM, activity with explicit N/A reporting for unexposed sensors), configurable test suites, zero-disk-roundtrip GPU VRAM ray tracing viewport inspection with split/diff/heatmap views, interactive Empirical Roofline log-log charts, and unified v2.0 JSON session import/comparison/export.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display program version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-backend " \fIBACKEND\fR"
Select default compute backend: auto, vulkan, opencl, rocm.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group ", " \-\-groups " \fINAMES\fR"
Benchmark group(s) to enable: compute, memory, scheduling, graphics (combines raster & raytracing), raster, raytracing, system, all.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-benchmark ", " \-\-benchmarks " \fIBENCHMARKS\fR"
Specific benchmark(s) to enable (comma-separated). Supported identifiers include: fp32, fp64, dualissue, lds, indirect, fp16, bf16, fp8, fp6, fp4, int8, int4, sparsematrix, coopvector, membw, interconnect, l0_cache, cache_latency_curve, asyncoverlap, workgraphs, pixelfill, rayrawtraversal, rayasbuild, rayintersect, rayanyhit, rayomm, rayprocedural, raypayload, rayscheduling, raydivergence, sysmembw, sysmemlatency, all.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " \fIDEVICES\fR"
Target GPU device index(es) (e.g., 0, 1, 0,1, dual, or all).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-scene " \fISCENE\fR"
Pre-select Ray Tracing scene: showroom, indoor, outdoor, forest, or all.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-res ", " \-\-resolution " \fIPRESET\fR"
Resolution preset: auto, 720p, 1080p, 1440p, 4k, 8k, or custom WxH.
.TP
.BR \-\-spp " \fISPP\fR"
Samples per pixel for ray tracing accumulation (1..256).
.TP
.BR \-\-ui-scale ", " \-\-scale " \fISCALE\fR"
Override UI DPI scaling factor (e.g., 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 2.0).
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-renders ", " \-\-dump
Enable saving rendered PNG comparison frames to disk (\fIrenders/\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-no-dump-renders ", " \-\-no-dump
Disable saving rendered output images to disk (renders remain viewable directly in GPU VRAM via the shared Vulkan 1.4 device).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-import ", " \-\-input " \fIFILE\fR"
Load a unified v2.0 or v1.x JSON report into the GUI session on startup.
.TP
.BR \-\-compare " \fIFILE\fR"
Load a baseline JSON report for side-by-side delta comparison in the Results Scorecard.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output-json " \fIFILE\fR"
Automatically export unified v2.0 JSON results upon benchmark completion.
.TP
.BR \-\-roofline
Open the Empirical Roofline tab automatically after loading or completing a run.
.TP
.BR \-\-screenshot " \fIPATH\fR"
Capture the rendered GUI swapchain to a PNG image before exiting.
.TP
.BR \-\-auto-run ", " \-\-auto-start ", " \-\-run
Automatically begin benchmark execution immediately upon launch.
.TP
.BR \-\-exit-on-complete
Exit automatically when the benchmark run finishes.
.TP
.BR \-\-frames " \fICOUNT\fR"
Run for the specified number of frames and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging output.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable Vulkan validation layers and debug logging output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch GUI with Vulkan backend, Ray Tracing group, and GPU 0 selected:
.B gpubench-gui \-k vulkan \-g raytracing \-d 0
.TP
Launch GUI with Compute and Memory benchmarks at 1080p:
.B gpubench-gui \-g compute,memory \-r 1080p
.TP
Run Ray Scheduling benchmark automatically and dump renders:
.B gpubench-gui \-b rayscheduling \-\-dump-renders \-\-auto-run
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpubench (1)
